markdown <<MARKDOWN
# Guiding Students through Coding Levels 

<img src="https://images.code.org/53796bf2dca42a298321692071188a94-image-1777991333557.png" alt="icon of a student with question marks" width="150px" style="border-radius:10px; float:right; margin: 0 80px 0px 20px;">

Students sometimes need support when coding with AI. Some common struggles are: 
- Skip reading the existing code
- Don’t understand the context
- Jump straight to asking AI

## Steps for success

This protocol helps students understand the starter code, describe the feature they want to build, and use AI as a support tool while working with JavaScript.

<div style="width:100%; max-width:760px; margin:20px 0px;">

  <details style="margin-bottom:14px;">
    <summary style="cursor:pointer; list-style:none; background-color:#B7E0E5; color:#000000; padding:10px 14px; border-radius:10px;">
      <span style="font-size:18pt; font-weight:bold;">🔍 Understand the Starter Code</span>
    </summary>
    <div style="background:#F5F7F8; border-radius:0 0 10px 10px; padding:12px 16px;">
      <p style="font-size:14pt; line-height:1.3; margin:0 0 8px 0;">Help students notice what data, buttons, functions, and display areas already exist.</p>
      <p style="font-size:14pt; line-height:1.3; margin:0;">Encourage them to ask, “What is this code already doing before I change it?”</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details style="margin-bottom:14px;">
    <summary style="cursor:pointer; list-style:none; background-color:#B7E0E5; color:#000000; padding:10px 14px; border-radius:10px;">
      <span style="font-size:18pt; font-weight:bold;">📌 Locate the TODO Task</span>
    </summary>
    <div style="background:#F5F7F8; border-radius:0 0 10px 10px; padding:12px 16px;">
      <p style="font-size:14pt; line-height:1.3; margin:0 0 8px 0;">Direct students to the TODO comments that show where a function, event listener, or logic needs to be added.</p>
      <p style="font-size:14pt; line-height:1.3; margin:0;">Have them point to the exact place where their new JavaScript code should go.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details style="margin-bottom:14px;">
    <summary style="cursor:pointer; list-style:none; background-color:#B7E0E5; color:#000000; padding:10px 14px; border-radius:10px;">
      <span style="font-size:18pt; font-weight:bold;">🧠 Plan the Behavior in Words</span>
    </summary>
    <div style="background:#F5F7F8; border-radius:0 0 10px 10px; padding:12px 16px;">
      <p style="font-size:14pt; line-height:1.3; margin:0 0 8px 0;">Before writing code, have students describe what should happen when the user interacts with the app.</p>
      <p style="font-size:14pt; line-height:1.3; margin:0;">For example: “When the user clicks the button, show only posts with more than 100 likes.”</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details style="margin-bottom:14px;">
    <summary style="cursor:pointer; list-style:none; background-color:#B7E0E5; color:#000000; padding:10px 14px; border-radius:10px;">
      <span style="font-size:18pt; font-weight:bold;">🤖 Prompt the AI</span>
    </summary>
    <div style="background:#F5F7F8; border-radius:0 0 10px 10px; padding:12px 16px;">
      <p style="font-size:14pt; line-height:1.3; margin:0 0 8px 0;">Support students in writing a clear prompt that explains the context, goal, constraints, and output expectations.</p>
      <p style="font-size:14pt; line-height:1.3; margin:0;">For JavaScript features, students should include the data being used, the user action, the condition or rule, and what should change on the screen.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details style="margin-bottom:14px;">
    <summary style="cursor:pointer; list-style:none; background-color:#B7E0E5; color:#000000; padding:10px 14px; border-radius:10px;">
      <span style="font-size:18pt; font-weight:bold;">🔁 Test and Refine</span>
    </summary>
    <div style="background:#F5F7F8; border-radius:0 0 10px 10px; padding:12px 16px;">
      <p style="font-size:14pt; line-height:1.3; margin:0 0 8px 0;">Encourage students to run the program, interact with the feature, and check whether the behavior matches their plan.</p>
      <p style="font-size:14pt; line-height:1.3; margin:0;">Students should expect to adjust their code, revise their prompt, and test again as they improve the feature.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

</div>





> #### As you work through these coding levels, practice using these steps yourself. Notice how clear planning and prompting improve the AI’s responses, and think about how you will model and scaffold this process for your students.

## Let's get started! 
 
